      "created_at": "2026-03-02T13:17:50.737Z",
      "cooked": "<p>In the <strong>User DocType → Settings → List Settings</strong>, there is an option called <strong>“Bulk Actions.”</strong></p>\n<p>My understanding is that if this option is unchecked for a user, then:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>The checkbox column in List View should disappear.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>The “Actions” dropdown should not appear.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Multi-select bulk operations should be disabled.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>However, even after unchecking <strong>Bulk Actions</strong> for the user:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>The checkbox column is still visible.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>The “Actions” button still appears in List View.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Bulk operations remain accessible.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>My questions:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>\n<p>What exactly does “Bulk Actions” in User → List Settings control?</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Is there an additional setting required for it to take effect?</p>\n</li>\n</ol>\n<p>Any clarification on how this setting is supposed to work would be appreciated.</p>",
